Apple offers two versions of the <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/09/09/airpods-5-announced-improved-anc/">AirPods 5</a>: a &#36;129 model with a USB-C Charging Case and a &#36;149 model with a Wireless Charging Case. The extra &#36;20 also buys longer battery life, swipe volume controls, and additional Find My features, so there are differences between the earbuds themselves as well as their cases.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/09/airpods-5-new-blue.jpeg" alt="" width="2500" height="1406" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1066076" /><br/>
Both models include <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/09/09/airpods-5-include-anc-as-standard/">Active Noise Cancellation as standard</a>, the H2 chip, the same open-ear design, and the same redesigned acoustic architecture with updated Adaptive EQ. They also share Transparency mode, Adaptive Audio, Conversation Awareness, Personalized Spatial Audio, Voice Isolation, studio-quality audio recording, and IP57 dust, sweat, and water resistance. Both support Live Translation when paired with a compatible iPhone with Apple Intelligence enabled, in supported languages and regions.<br/>
<br/>
The earbuds have identical dimensions and weight. The cases are also the same size, although the Wireless Charging Case is slightly heavier. There are still some notable differences to justify the price difference. Our guide helps to answer the question of how to decide which of these sets of AirPods is best for you.<br/>
